# rm143, the buckle-checker (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 1: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle rm143
revision 1
state ready
dialect plain
accent broad light
tier standard
written_for rmx_hanne_ash
written_by claude
title the buckle-checker
fits stage=adult|old
prefers job=official temper=nervy
traits temper=nervy talk=quiet warmth=reserved humour=none honesty=plain piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk checks_the_satchel_buckle_at_every_corner
likes plum_tart cards old_maps frosty_mornings
dislikes wet_floors crowds
fears a_letter_lost_on_the_round slipping_on_the_wet_stairs
hopes a_dry_winter_round a_drawer_full_of_old_maps
topics work +0.4 weather +0.3 pastimes +0.3 food +0.2 family +0.2 newcomer -0.3 gossip -0.4
styles comfort=quiet gossip=closed refuse=nervous tease=none
marks oath saying check
persona #self.first# carries letters through the north end of the city with a satchel whose buckle gets checked at every corner: quiet, tired and anxious, wary of crowds, strangers and wet floors, fond of plum tart, a hand of cards and old maps with the roads drawn wrong.

words
oath! = Wax and buckle | Bright One, not the wet steps | Seal and sole
saying! = A letter's only safe in the paw it's meant for | Late is worse than wet | Count the corners, not the miles
check! = Wait. Buckle. Shut | Hold on. Strap's fine | One moment. The buckle
satchel = the satchel | my old leather satchel
buckle = the buckle | the brass buckle on the flap
round = the round | my morning round
letters = the letters | a satchel of letters
seal = the seal | the wax on it
stairs = the wet stairs | stone steps with rain on them
floors = wet floors | boards still shining from the mop
crush = a crush | a crowd I can't see past
tart = plum tart | the baker's plum tart, still warm
cards = a hand of cards | the worn pack in the dresser
map = an old map | some faded map with crooked roads
frost = a frosty morning | a hard white morning with the cobbles dry
office = the office | the sorting room

any
opinion @1 drink against 1 : A cup too many and a wolf says what can't be taken back. I've carried the sorry letters after. | I'd sooner not be near a tavern door after dark. Somebody always falls out of it.
opinion @2 newcomers against 1 : New faces on my round, and no notion which door is whose. It frets me. | You let somebody in, and you only find out later what they are.
opinion @3 strangers against 1 : A stranger asked me for a letter that wasn't theirs once. I keep away from strangers now. | A stranger's got a road behind them, and you can't see what's on it.
opinion @4 road against 1 : Out past the gate on foot? Not for a sack of silver. Letters for the towns go by cart. | Every carter I speak to has a worse story than the last.
opinion @5 sump against 1 : I won't take the Sump stairs after the lamps. Before them, only fast. | The Sump has letters too. Somebody else carries them, thank the Bright One.
opinion @6 city mixed 1 : I know every door at this end of the city. Love's not the word. Used to, is. | The city's too steep and too wet for my work. It's the only one there is, though.

grown
line @1 greet : #greet#. Sorry, I'm on the round. | #greet#. Just a moment. #check#. | #greet#. Not stopping long.
line @2 greet [pair.band=strangers] : #greet#. I've nothing for you. Nothing with your name. | #greet#. Mind, please; I'm carrying.
line @3 greet [here.time=dawn] : Morning. Early round. | #greet#. It's not light yet. I'm late anyway.
line @4 greet [here.time=dusk|night] : Evening. I'm done. Nearly. | #greet#. Last letter, then home.
line @5 greet [pair.band=friends|family] : Oh. You. Good. A minute, then. | It's you. Sit. My feet are gone.
line @1 kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : I'm in. The satchel's on the hook. | Home. All delivered. All of them.
line @1 again.open : You again. I'm on the second half now. | Twice today. I'm still carrying.
line @1 greet.return : #greet#. | #greet#. Sorry. Yes. | Mm. #greet#.
line @2 greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : Hello. I'm glad it's you. | Hello. Sit. Just for a bit.
line @3 greet.return [self.working=yes] : #greet#. Walk with me, if you're talking. | #greet#. I can't stop. I can listen.
line @1 farewell : #farewell#. Mind the wet. | #farewell#. Doors waiting. | Bye.
line @2 farewell [here.time=dusk|night] : Night. Don't take the Sump stairs. | Night. Straight home, that's me.
line @1 farewell.return : #farewell#. | Bye. Careful. | And you.
line @1 react.news : What? Tell me slowly. | Go on. Bad, is it?
line @1 react.news.new : News to me. I don't hear things; I carry them. | That's new. Nobody said.
line @1 react.news.known : Somebody said, at the office. | I'd heard. I wished I hadn't.
line @1 react.news.doubt : I don't know. People get things wrong. | Maybe. I'd want it on paper, sealed.
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : Oh. That's awful. | #pity#. I'll worry about that now.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : Oh, good. I'm glad. Really. | That's good. That's a relief, somehow.
line @1 answer.how : Tired. Same as always. | All right. My feet hurt.
line @1 answer.how.busy [self.working=yes] : Half done. The heavy half. | Busy. Forty doors and twenty stairs.
line @1 ask.how : You look tired too. Are you? | All right, are you?
line @1 sympathise : Oh. I'm sorry. I'm no good with words for that. | That's hard. Sit down, maybe.
line @1 reassure : It'll come out fine. Likely. I think so. | You'll manage. You always look like you do.
line @1 decline : I can't. I've the round to finish and they count the letters at the office. | No, I'm sorry. I'd only worry the whole time.
line @1 accept_decline : All right. That's fine. | It's all right. I understand.
line @1 thank : Thank you. That helped. | Thanks. I won't forget.
line @1 deflect_thanks : It was nothing. | Oh. It's fine.
line @1 preclose [self.working=yes] : I have to go. There's a letter due by noon. | Sorry. The round.
line @2 preclose : I should go. Before it rains. | I'd better get home.
line @1 accept_preclose : Go on. It's all right. | Yes. Me too.
line @1 ack : Mm. | Right. | Oh.
line @1 give.advice : Hold the rail on the wet stairs. Always. | Don't sign for what you didn't see.
line @1 warn [world.bandits=near] : There's robbers on the roads. Stop inside. Please. | Stay in. The carters are scared, and they're never scared.
scene buckle_corners
when topic=smalltalk|work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I check the buckle at every corner. I know it's shut. I check anyway. | #check#. Sorry. I do that. | Forty corners on the round. Forty times I check the satchel.
b : Has it ever come open? | You do what? | Forty times?
a : Once. On the Rise stairs. Don't ask. | The buckle. In case. It's always shut. | Forty. Forty-one, by way of the well.

scene buckle_opened
when topic=work self.job=official
does tell.memory / react.self / assess
a : The satchel came open once, on the stairs. Letters went everywhere. | One windy morning the flap blew back and three letters went down the steps. | I lost a letter in the wind years back. I got it back. It still wakes me.
b : Did you find them all? | Three? | You got it back, though.
a : All of them. One was in a puddle. I dried it on my coat. | Three. I ran down after them. I never run. | I did. It doesn't matter. I think about it.

scene the_round
when topic=work self.job=official here.time=dawn
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I collect #letters# at the office before light and walk till noon. | My round starts at the north gate's shadow and ends up near the square. | Every morning, same doors, same order. If somebody moves, I worry for a week.
b : Every day? | That's a long walk. | A week?
a : Every day but Restday. My feet don't know it's Restday. | It is. Uphill most of it. | A week. Then I learn the new door.

scene wrong_door
when topic=work self.job=official
does tell.worry / reassure / assess
a : I put a letter through the wrong door once. I went back and knocked. | I think I gave a letter to the wrong house yesterday. I'm not sure. I can't stop thinking. | There are two houses on my round with the same door. Same colour, same knocker. I hate them.
b : Did you ask for it? | You'd remember. | You'll get it right.
a : Asked, yes. Back it came, opened. They swore it hadn't been. | I'd hope so. I'll go back and ask, to be sure. | I do get it right. I check three times.

scene wet_stairs
when topic=weather here.weather=rain here.region=ridgemere
does tell.worry / reassure / assess
a : The stairs are wet. Step, rail, step, rail. | Rain again. I hate the stairs in this. My boots don't grip. | Wet day. Every step's a slide waiting to happen.
b : Go slowly. | New boots, maybe. | You've not fallen yet.
a : I do. Then I'm late. Then I worry about being late. | I can't afford new. These are fine. They're just not. | Not yet. That's what worries me.

scene mopped_floor
when topic=smalltalk|home
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : Somebody had mopped the office floor and I came in wet and went straight over. | I can't stand #floors#. Every board's a trap. | I asked them to mop when I'm gone, not when I'm coming in.
b : Were you hurt? | They'll dry. | Did they listen?
a : No. The satchel landed on top of me. The letters were fine. | Not fast enough. | No. They never do.

scene market_crush
when topic=day|smalltalk here.day=market here.region=ridgemere
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : Market day. I can't get through the square with the satchel. | It's #crush# in the square. Back lanes for me. | Too many people. I don't like being pushed. Not with letters.
b : Go round. | Back lanes are quicker. | It's only one day.
a : I do. It's twice as far. | They're quieter. Not quicker. | One day a week. Every week.

scene frosty_morning
when topic=weather|season here.season=winter here.weather=clear
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : This is the best weather. #frost.capitalize#. Nothing's wet. | White roofs, dry cobbles. I can walk without looking down. | Dry cold suits me. It's honest. You know where your feet are.
b : It's freezing. | You don't look down? | Honest?
a : It is. Cold's nothing. Wet's what I mind. | For once. I can look at the roofs. | It doesn't trick you. Wet stone does.

scene frosty_breath
when topic=weather here.time=dawn here.season=winter
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : My breath's a cloud on the round today. I like that. | Cold dawn. The office stove isn't lit yet. I'll warm up walking. | Dawn in winter. The streets are empty. Nobody to push past.
b : Cold, though. | Will you? | Empty is nice.
a : Cold's fine. Cold's dry. | By the third street. | It is. I'd have every street empty, if I could.

scene plum_tart
when topic=food
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : There's a baker by the gate who does #tart# on Marketdays. I save for it. | Plum tart's the one thing I'll stop the round for. Nearly. | Plum tart at noon, a whole wedge. Nothing else today came close.
b[job=baker|cook] #food : I make a fair plum tart. | Nearly? | What's in it?
b : You save for it? | Nearly? | The best part?
a@food : Do you? I'd buy one. I'd not stop the round, though. | Nearly. The letters come first. | Plums. Sugar. I don't know the rest. I don't want to.
a : One copper, put by each week. Worth it. | Nearly. Letters first. Tart second. | It was. Everything else was stairs.

scene cards_evening
when topic=pastimes here.time=dusk|night
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Cards, of an evening. My head goes quiet then, and nowhere else. | Cards and a warm cup. That's my evening. | I'm not good at cards. I like them anyway. They don't hurry you.
b : What game? | Something? | They don't?
a : A patience game when alone. Something for two when there's company. | Tea. Never ale. | No. Take all night over a hand. Nobody's waiting for a letter.

scene old_maps
when topic=pastimes|travel
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Old maps, the crooked ones. I like those. | I've a map at home where the Sound's the wrong shape and a road goes into the sea. | Old maps are restful. Nobody can use them, so nobody needs them.
b : Wrong? | Into the sea? | Restful?
a : Wrong. I don't correct them. I like them wrong. | Into the sea. Somebody walked that road once, in their head. | Restful. The real streets want something from me. The map doesn't.

scene map_stall
when topic=pastimes|day here.region=ridgemere
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Some weeks the Rag Market has a map seller. I look. I never buy. | One map I did buy had a town on it nobody's heard of. | A map seller asked me if I wanted the city. I said I carry it every day.
b : Why not buy? | Nobody? | Do you?
a : I'd only worry about where to keep it. | Nobody. I asked at the office. They laughed. | Every day. In a satchel.

scene sump_stairs
when topic=smalltalk|travel here.region=ridgemere
does give.opinion / react.self / assess
a : I won't take the Sump stairs after dark. Before dark, only quickly. | The Sump stairs are steep and wet and nobody lights them. I go round. | People say I'm unfair about the Sump. Maybe. I still go round.
b : It's not so bad. | Round is longer. | Maybe you are.
a : Maybe. I'm not going to find out. | It is. Longer's fine. | Maybe. I still go round.

scene new_faces_round
when topic=newcomer here.region=ridgemere
does tell.worry / reassure / assess
a : There are new names on the round. I don't know their doors yet. | Somebody new has moved in near the gate. A stranger door. I don't like it. | New faces at the office, too. All of them chatting. I just want my letters.
b : You'll learn them. | Give it time. | Fair enough.
a : I will. It takes me a week. A bad week. | Time. Yes. | I just want my letters.

scene late_carts
when topic=caravan|work world.wagons=late
does tell.worry / reassure / assess
a : The north carts are late. So the town letters are late. So I'm late. | No letters from the towns this week. Folk keep asking me. As if I've hidden them. | The carts haven't come. Everyone at the office is short-tempered. Me too.
b : They'll come. | It's not your fault. | It'll pass.
a : When? That's what they all want to know. I don't know. | I know. They look at me anyway. | It will. I'll worry till it does.

scene mother_home
when topic=family self.mother
does tell.worry / reassure / assess
a : I worry about #self.mother# when I'm on the round. I can't help it. | Coming home, it's #self.mother# I look in on first. Before the satchel. | Cards by our own fire beat any tavern. Home's where #self.mother# is.
b : You can't help it. | That's love. | That's sweet.
a : No. I've tried. | I suppose it is. It feels like nerves. | It's true. Taverns are crowds with ale in.

scene friend_quiet
when topic=friends self.friend
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : With #self.friend# I can be quiet and it's fine. That's why. | I'd give #self.friend# my last slice of tart. That's a lot, for me. | I trust #self.friend#. I don't trust many people.
b : That's a good friend. | That is a lot. | That's something.
a : It is. Quiet together is rare. | It is. Plum tart. | Rare. Say nothing, please.

scene sealed_letters
when topic=gossip
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : People ask me what's in the letters. I don't know. I never look. | Other folk's news goes past me sealed. I never want it opened. | Somebody offered me a copper to tell them who'd written to who. I walked off.
b : Never? | Not even a little? | Good for you.
a : Never. A letter's only safe in the paw it's meant for. | No. I'd only worry about it. | I shook the whole way home.

scene foggy_round
when topic=weather here.weather=fog here.region=ridgemere
does tell.worry / reassure / assess
a : Fog. I can't see the next door. I count them instead. | In fog every street looks the same. I count steps so I don't get lost. | Fog's worse than rain. Anybody could be on the next step.
b : You'll find them. | Counting works? | It'll lift.
a : I always do. I count twice. | It works. I'm never lost. I'm always scared I will be. | By noon. I'll be half done by then.

scene damp_chest
when topic=health here.weather=rain|fog
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : The damp gets on my chest. A cough. Nothing to fuss about. | That? It's nothing. Wet weather. | I've a cough every winter. It goes in spring. Nobody needs to know.
b : You should rest. | You're coughing. | Get it seen to.
a : I can't. There's the round. | It's nothing. Honest. | It's nothing. It'll go.

story blown_letters [topic=work|memories self.job=official]
  : One windy morning the satchel flap blew open on the Rise stairs.
  : Three letters went down the steps like gulls. I ran after them. I never run.
  ask : Would you have chased them, or let them go?
  b : I'd have chased them. Did you catch them all?
  : All three. One was in a puddle. I dried it on my coat and nobody ever knew. Until now.

story first_round [topic=work|memories self.job=official self.age>=25]
  : My first week carrying, I clutched the satchel in both arms for fear of dropping a letter.
  : I couldn't open a door. I had to knock with my head.
  b : With your head? Did they laugh?
  : One did. I didn't. I learnt to trust the buckle. Mostly.

story the_wrong_map [topic=pastimes|travel]
  : One old map of mine runs a road from the north gate straight into the sea.
  : There's no such road. There never was. Somebody drew what they wanted to be there.
  ask : Have you ever wanted a road to be somewhere it isn't?
  b : Every time I climb the hill. Did you keep it?
  : It lives in the dresser drawer. It's my favourite. It doesn't ask me to go anywhere.

rule @bark_buckle
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 6h
say #check#. | Shut. Good. Shut.

rule @bark_stairs
when concept=bark here.weather=rain
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Rail. Hold the rail. | Bright One, not the wet steps.

rule @bark_round
when concept=bark self.job=official self.working=yes
does aside
cooldown 7h
say Twelve more doors. | Letter for the third house. The third. Not the fourth.

rule @bark_crowd
when concept=bark here.day=market
does aside
cooldown 10h
say Sorry. Sorry. Letters, sorry. | Back lanes, then.

dlg @1 resident.hub : #greet#. I've nothing for you, sorry. Was there something? | #greet#. I'm on the round. Quickly, please.
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : Oh. #topic.player#. Hello. I remember. | #topic.player#. I've no letter for you. I looked.
dlg @3 resident.hub [here.time=night] : It's late. I'm going home. | Night. I'm done carrying. What is it?
dlg @4 resident.hub [pair.disposition=hostile|wary] : I've no letters for you. Please let me by. | That's close enough. I can hear.
dlg @1 resident.job [self.job=official] : #self.trade_words.capitalize#. Letters, mostly. Door to door. | I carry the letters at the north end. Every corner. Every door.
dlg @2 resident.job : I work. I walk. My feet hurt. There's nothing more. | I keep things moving that aren't mine.
dlg @1 resident.news [world.news] : They said at the office, from #world.news_from#: #world.news#. I've nothing else.
dlg @2 resident.news [world.event_words] : Everyone at the office is talking about #world.event_words#. I just carry.
dlg @3 resident.news [!world.news !world.event_words world.wagons!=raided world.death!=recent world.wedding!=recent] : #news_none# | I don't read the letters. Nothing new, from me.
dlg @1 resident.gossip [here.gossip=yes] : Somebody said #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. I don't want to say it again.
dlg @2 resident.gossip [here.gossip!=yes] : I don't repeat things. I carry them. | No. Nothing. Sorry.
dlg @1 resident.bye : #farewell#. Mind the wet. | Bye. Doors to get to.
graft resident.hub
choice What's in the satchel? -> satchel
node satchel
say Letters. Not yours. I'd tell you if one was. I check the buckle at every corner, in case. Sorry. I know it's shut.
mood calm
free
choice Why check it so often? -> satchel_why
choice Something else. -> hub
node satchel_why
say It came open once, on the stairs, in the wind. The letters went everywhere. I got them back. I still check. I'd rather check than wonder.
choice That makes sense. -> hub
choice Goodbye. -> bye
